\mt1 Numbers
c 24
\v 2  … The Spirit of God came upon Balaam,
\v 3 and he took up his parable and said, …
\v 5 ‘How beautiful are your dwellings, O Jacob, and your tents, O Israel. 
\v 6 They are as shaded valleys, and gardens by a river, and as tents which the Lord pitched, and cedars beside the waters.
\v 7 From his offspring shall come a man who will rule over many nations; and his kingdom will be exalted and will increase.
\v 8 God led him out of Egypt; to him he was like the glory of a unicorn. He will devour the nations of his enemies, and he will suck out the marrow of their fatness, and shoot down the enemy with his darts.
\v 9 He lay down and took his rest like a lion, like a young lion; who would rouse him? Blessed are those who bless you, and cursed are those who curse you.
\v 17 A star shall rise from Jacob, and a man shall arise out of Israel. He will crush the princes of Moab, and plunder all the children of Seth.
\v 18 Edom shall be an inheritance; and Esau, his enemy, shall be an inheritance; and Israel acted with strength.

